# SHA-256 of upstream's scripts/setup-periphery.py, per Komodo version. Read by
# scripts/upgrade-periphery.sh, which REFUSES to publish a version it has no pin for.
#
# Why pin at all: today a host runs that script as root having fetched it from
# raw.githubusercontent.com with no verification whatsoever (bootstrap/onboard-host.sh:37). The
# pin plus serving it from the manager replaces "trust the network" with "trust this hash", and
# it is the same idiom bootstrap/secaudit/versions.env already uses for lynis and docker-bench.
#
# To add a version: run `scripts/upgrade-periphery.sh --pin` and commit the line it prints. It
# never records a hash by itself — an auto-recorded pin verifies nothing — but it does cross-check
# for you: it compares the GIT BLOB SHA-1 of what it downloaded against what GitHub's API says the
# tag points at. The raw CDN and the API are different endpoints, so agreement between them is a
# statement about the repository rather than about what one server chose to serve.
#
# v2.3.2 pinned 2026-09-09. sha256 below; git blob 425373ba7f037b0e6be9c1c7d8bfaf0d4f4abf23,
# 7450 bytes, and the API confirmed that blob for tag v2.3.2.
SETUP_PERIPHERY_v2_3_2_SHA256=f7e81889d7bda62f627d4b87cf6ac3ecb943db7bcbf40a22faec4c660d8b80f1
